<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.3.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01773</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.3.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>1b4b0aee-b084-4bf9-8eae-102d7d1b2bb2</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Sketch or describe the figure in Step 4 and Step 15.<figure><media alt="Three steps of a growing pattern"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/7af9c38ee51b4d3864f92f32f049e74eb31e64ad"/></media></figure></item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item> How many small squares are in Step 4? </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 16</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item> How many small squares are in Step 15? </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 225</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item> Which equation represents the relationship between the step number, \(n\), and the number of small squares, \(y\), in each step.<list>
        <item> \(y=n^2\) </item>
        <item>\(
          y=n^2+1\) </item>
        <item> \(y=n^2-1\) </item>
        <item> \(y=n^2-n\) </item>
      </list>
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(y=n^2\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Each figure is composed of large squares and small squares. The side length of the large square is \(x\). Choose the correct expression that represents the area, \(y\), of the shaded part of each figure.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item> Figure A <figure><media alt="Large square with 1 by 1 small squares removed from each corner."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/6f4278bac2d8a892bcfce054c9da28e0ad241e1d"/></media></figure><list>
        <item>\(
          y=x^2\) </item>
        <item> \(y=x^2-1\) </item>
        <item>\(y=x^2-4\) </item>
        <item> \(y=x^2-8\) </item>
      </list>
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(y=x^2-4\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item>Figure B<figure><media alt="2 large squares side by side. On the side of the right square, there are 2 small squares stacked vertically, each with dimensions 2 by 2."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/054192d3c001b09c3745696ad0c2632da9ef6b91"/></media></figure><list>
        <item> \(y=x^2\) </item>
        <item> \(y=2x^2+8\) </item>
        <item> \(y=x^2+8\) </item>
        <item> \(y=2x^2\) </item>
      </list>
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(y=2x^2+8\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Use the sequence below to answer a and b.</item>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt="DIAGRAM WITH 3 FIGURES, SHOWING STEPS 1 THROUGH 3. STEP 1 HAS A RECTANGLE WITH 1 ROW AND 2 COLUMNS. 1 SQUARE IS ADDED TO THE TOP RIGHT. STEP 2 HAS A RECTANGLE WITH 2 ROWS AND 3 COLUMNS. 2 SQUARES ARE ADDED TO THE TOP RIGHT. STEP 3 HAS A RECTANGLE WITH 3 ROWS AND 4 COLUMNS. 3 SQUARES ARE ADDED TO THE TOP RIGHT."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b4c3cb9433e614fd5a11d44143280aa228c70485"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item> How many squares are in Step 5? </item>
  </list>
</list>
<emphasis> </emphasis>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>35</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item> Choose the correct expression that represents the area, \(y\), of the shaded part of each figure for \(n\) steps.<list>
        <item> \(n-1\) </item>
        <item> \(n^2-1\) </item>
        <item> \((n+1)^2\) </item>
        <item> \((n+1)^2-1\) </item>
      </list>
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((n+1)^2-1\)</para></section>
</content>
